From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 20:33:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Systematic audit fixes: security, tier/checker divergence,
 over-blocking, write-once credential UI
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fixes every real finding from this session's own 8-agent audit (registry-
consistency across all 4 products + adversarial code review of Phases 1-6),
plus the dedicated Showtime workers audit run after it.

Security (CRITICAL/HIGH):
- Klaviyo and HubSpot Conversations webhook routes: signature verification
  could be bypassed entirely by omitting headers, even with a secret
  configured. Now rejects (401) rather than silently skipping verification.
- Composio OAuth callback CSRF/account-linking vuln: no binding between a
  connect attempt and its callback beyond an ordinary session cookie. Adds
  a single-use, workspace-bound state token (new composio_connect_attempts
  table) validated and consumed before any credential is linked.
- /api/credentials/test: added missing workspaceId scoping to its ownership
  check (whopUserId alone let a caller probe another workspace's engagement).
- rotateComposioVaultCredential: reordered so the DB write happens before
  revoking the old connection, so a DB failure can't orphan a vault row.

Win-Back auto-pause (esp-delivery-monitor.ts): fixed a race condition (now
an atomic compare-and-swap instead of read-then-write), partial-failure
masking (DB status only flips for enrollments whose ESP exit actually
succeeded), and permanent stranding (every call re-sweeps stragglers, not
just the first pause-triggering one). Narrowed the SMTP bounce-detection
regex to drop phrases with real false-positive risk in genuine replies.

Tier/checker divergence (worker-registry.ts / worker-config-completeness.ts):
corrected rep-onboarding's competitors/trustedSources/entities and
icp-lock's productPrice — all tiered "blocking" but never actually enforced
by their real checkers, per this session's own registry-consistency audits.

Over-blocking (worker-config-completeness.ts): pile-on's smsA2p10dlcStatus/
smsComplianceFooterVariant and pre-call-read's 4 opt-in credentials were
tiered "deferrable" but blocked the ENTIRE worker run the moment an
operator opted into the feature, contradicting the tier's own documented
semantics and duplicating safety nets that already exist at the point of
use (sendSmsForTenant's per-send A2P guard, brief-service.ts's per-source
try/catch soft-fails). Removed from the full-run checkers; capability-
status readers untouched since the Live Capability Matrix should still
show these as missing.

Write-once credential UI (credentials.ts, new syncStackCredentialMarkers):
the post-creation "Update Credentials" UI (CredentialRow) only ever wrote
credentialsRefs — the completeness checkers and capability-status readers
actually gate on a separate stack.*_credentials_ref marker that nothing
in that UI ever touched, so a client whose credential wasn't captured at
creation time could connect a real key, get a success toast, and stay
permanently blocked. Wired into /api/credentials and
/api/engagements/[id]/credentials/link.

Capability-status reader conditionals (worker-capability-status.ts): fixed
pin-down's hostingPlatformCredential, pile-on's smsA2p10dlcStatus and
adDataPlatformCredential to mirror their real checkers' platform-specific
conditionals, matching the pattern leak-map/win-back's readers already used.

Minor: daily-send's Save button now enforces the same 500/day upper bound
the backend does; HeldLeadsPanel's fetch effect now guards against setting
state after unmount; send-connect/source-connect readers now import
coldOpenCredentialProvider instead of hand-duplicating the provider-key
string; stale header comments in worker-config-completeness.ts updated to
reflect that aging_threshold_days/refund-dispute thresholds/
REPORT_WINDOW_DAYS all got real schema slots in Phase 6.

Generated the composio_connect_attempts migration (drizzle-kit generate).
Updated 2 tests (smtp-bounce-classifier, esp-delivery-monitor) that had
gone stale against already-applied behavior changes from earlier this
session — full vitest run now matches the established baseline exactly
(59 failed/210 passed/18 skipped, all remaining failures a pre-existing
Next.js 16 cookies()-outside-request-scope test-harness gap unrelated to
this work). tsc clean, build compiles and typechecks clean.

