Subject: [PATCH] rep-onboarding gets the narrated flow it was missing
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

rep-onboarding already had the Live Capability Matrix and Inferred Cards
(Phase 3) but never the Progressive Flow every other configured worker on
the platform has gotten — flagged in review as one of the real gaps.

identity-graph-form.tsx: split its single long scroll into 3 named
sections (Operator, Watch list, Sources & panel) and added a `layout`
prop — "flat" (default, unchanged) keeps new/page.tsx's onboarding wizard
exactly as it was; "steps" wraps the same 3 sections in ProgressiveFlow
instead. Added onFinish/finishLabel/finishDisabled/finishing passthrough
so the caller's real save() becomes ProgressiveFlow's own finish button
in steps mode, replacing a separate Save button rather than duplicating
it. rep-onboarding-config-form.tsx now passes layout="steps" and its
existing handleSubmit — no change to what gets saved or how completeness
is validated, same canSave logic, just relocated into finishDisabled.

No field, state, save-payload, or validation logic changed — pure layout
retrofit, same approach every other Phase 3/5 worker got.

tsc clean, vitest unchanged at the established baseline (59 failed/210
passed/18 skipped).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QVWhaC6hTtT9UCKS7Dub7w
