Final 2 of the 14 configured workers on the platform.

- leak-map-config-form.tsx: 2 steps (Schedule, Report delivery);
  auditOutputFormat SelectField -> ChoiceCardGroup.
- win-back-config-form.tsx: 2 steps (Reschedule & replies, Deliverability
  monitoring); rescheduleMode and inboundReplyMode SelectFields ->
  ChoiceCardGroup. The auto-pause and GHL-unsupported alert banners stay
  above the flow as status banners, not steps — they're not configuration
  decisions.

All state, load effects, and save() payloads unchanged.

This completes the full sweep: every one of the 14 workers on the
platform with a real config form now has real Phase 3/5 treatment —
pin-down, pre-call-read, icp-lock, rep-onboarding, pile-on,
voice-capture, source-connect, send-connect, daily-send, leak-map,
win-back, whop-cancellation-save-offer, and whop-bridge-manager all use
ProgressiveFlow + WorkerCapabilityMatrix (+ ChoiceCardGroup wherever a
field is a platform/mode pick); whop-connect — a single-credential form
with no multi-field capability map — got its own equivalent treatment
(vault-slot styling, a real Armed-state transition, its existing
scope-probe results reframed as a capability matrix) since ProgressiveFlow
would add a pointless single-step wrapper around one input. No worker
was skipped.

tsc clean, vitest unchanged at the established baseline (59 failed/210
passed/18 skipped) across the whole sweep.

