From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 14:09:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Real live-content previews for voice-capture and
 whop-cancellation-save-offer
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Extends the preview-first pattern past the original 3 workers (pin-down,
pre-call-read, icp-lock) to the 2 remaining cases where a real preview —
not a mockup — is actually possible: both workers assemble real content
from typed template fields, the same shape pin-down's confirmation-page
preview already uses.

- voice-capture-live-preview.tsx: renders touch 1's subject/body exactly
  the way copy-engine.ts's assembleUpload/applyGreetingAndSignOff does
  (re-implemented, not imported — copy-engine.ts pulls in @/lib/llm,
  server-only, must never ship to the client bundle).
- whop-cancellation-save-offer-live-preview.tsx: substitutes {discount}/
  {months} into the typed message exactly the way
  cancellation-save-offer-service.ts does at send time — verified the
  real code uses a single (non-global) .replace() per token and matched
  that exactly rather than "improving" it into a global replace.

Both fall back to labeled placeholder copy when the relevant fields are
still empty, same convention pin-down's preview already established.

tsc clean.

