Completes the preview-first gap analysis: pile-on, source-connect,
send-connect, daily-send, win-back, and whop-bridge-manager produce
nothing a content preview could show, but every one of them has real,
computable behavior the moment fields are filled in. Added a shared
BehaviorSummary component (behavior-summary.tsx) that renders a plain-
language translation of CURRENT form state into actual consequences —
computed live from real values, not invented, same honesty level as a
content preview, just narrower in form.

- pile-on: which SMS/ad-data channels are active and where leads go.
- source-connect: per-ICP source + daily cap, or an honest "nothing
  configured yet" when no row has an ICP.
- send-connect: platform, how many ICPs have a live campaign mapped, and
  which ICPs (if any) auto-push without review.
- daily-send: volume/schedule, copy mode, and whether live sending is
  actually on or every run stays a dry run.
- win-back: reschedule link behavior, no-show tagging, and what actually
  stops the recovery cadence.
- whop-bridge-manager: destination, real field-mapping count (or a
  friendly parse-error note instead of crashing on invalid JSON), and the
  retry/dead-letter policy.

All computed from existing state, no new fetches, no fake data.

tsc clean, vitest unchanged at the established baseline (59 failed/210
passed/18 skipped) — this completes the full preview-first extension
across all 14 configured workers: 3 already had it, 2 got real content
previews, 1 got a real live CRM dry-run, 6 got real behavior summaries,
and 2 (rep-onboarding, whop-connect) correctly have neither since neither
produces addressable content nor consequential per-field behavior beyond
what their existing treatment already shows.

